a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. Community;
c. educational institutions;
d. health institutions;
e. community social institutions; and
f. business world and other institutions.

Article 7

The Community is obliged and responsible for the Protection of Women and Children through Community participation activities in the Implementation of Protection of Women and Children in the form of:
a. providing information and/or reporting any occurrence of vulnerability risks and Violence that is known;
b. facilitating deliberation for consensus to create restorative justice for Children in conflict with the law through informal channels and carried out at the village/sub-district government level and institutional authorities;
c. identifying/early detection and initial handling of Children at risk;
d. mediation and guidance for families experiencing domestic Violence, domestic conflict, and divorce;
e. preparation of families and Communities in accepting Children who are victims of abuse and/or Children at risk; and
f. the process of repatriation, social Rehabilitation, and social Reintegration.

Pasal 22

The Regional Government is responsible for efforts to protect Women and Children from acts of Violence that occur in the form of:
a. physical Violence;
b. sexual Violence;
c. economic Violence;
d. social Violence;
e. psychological Violence;
f. domestic neglect;
g. coercion or deprivation of liberty; and h. threats of certain actions.

Pasal 19

1. The Regional Government plays a role in facilitating the handling of Children in conflict with the law.
2. the handling of Children in conflict with the law as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:
a. capacity building of government apparatus, social workers and the Community;
b. increased coordination with law enforcement officials;
c. provision of supporting facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of the juvenile criminal justice system;
d. development of effective methods through information support, facilities and positive activities as well as taking immediate action on gaps that encourage Children and/or groups of Children to commit legal violations;
e. provision and delivery of legal and psychosocial assistance services in realizing the process of restorative justice and diversion for Children in conflict with the law;
f. encouraging a paradigm shift in the Community towards Children in conflict with the law; and
g. developing diversion mechanisms for Children in conflict with the law in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.
3. The relevant SKPD responsible for social affairs and education shall organize social Rehabilitation and education for Children in conflict with the law in the form of:
a. provision of safe houses;
b. psychosocial Rehabilitation;
c. mental spiritual Rehabilitation;
d. fulfillment of the right to education; and
e. social Reintegration.

